                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_40\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit message explicitly describes two bugs in the FTS3 \"words\" table\nID-offsetting scheme used to distinguish sms rows from mms/part rows:\n\n1. In MmsProvider.java, the mms/part row ID was computed as `(2 << 32) + rowId`.\n   Because both operands of `<<` are `int` in Java, the shift amount is taken\n   modulo 32, so `2 << 32` evaluates to `2 << 0 == 2`, not the intended large\n   offset. This collides mms word IDs with sms word IDs.\n2. In MmsSmsDatabaseHelper.java, the `populateWordsTable` method (used to\n   backfill the words table on database upgrade) inserted mms/part rows using\n   the raw `id` from the Part table with no offset applied at all, so the\n   offsetting scheme was not applied there either.\n\nThe fix (fix_commit_diff.txt) changes the offset computation to\n`(1L << 33) + rowId` (using a long literal to avoid the int-shift bug) and adds\nthe missing `(1L << 33) + id` offset in `populateWordsTable`. It also removes\nthe now-unnecessary `SOURCE_ROW_ID`/`TABLE_ID` columns and switches all\ntriggers/queries to use the FTS3 rowid directly instead of those columns.\n\ncandidate_40 is the commit that originally introduced this entire \"words\"\ntable feature:\n- It adds `cv.put(Telephony.MmsSms.WordsTable.ID, (2 << 32) + rowId);` in\n  MmsProvider.java \u2014 the exact buggy int-shift expression named in the fix\n  commit message.\n- It adds the `populateWordsTable` method in MmsSmsDatabaseHelper.java, whose\n  mms/part branch inserts `cv.put(Telephony.MmsSms.WordsTable.ID, id);` with no\n  offset \u2014 the second bug described in the fix commit message (\"The\n  populateWordsTable method ... didn't add the offset at all\").\n- It also introduces `createWordsTables`, the `SOURCE_ROW_ID`/`TABLE_ID`\n  columns, and the `source_id`/`table_to_use`-based triggers/queries, all of\n  which are precisely what the fix commit removes/reworks.\n\nNo candidate prior to candidate_40 contains any reference to the words table,\n`WordsTable.ID`, `populateWordsTable`, `source_id`, or `table_to_use` (a\ntargeted search across all 136 candidates found matches only in candidate_40\nand later commits that touch/inherit this same code). This makes candidate_40\nthe first commit to introduce the problematic offsetting code, and therefore\nthe bug-introducing commit.\n"
